WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.999
When Bobby opened his eyes, everything looked the same.

2
00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:12.106
"Has my wish been granted?" he asked Huey.

3
00:00:12.107 --> 00:00:21.257
Huey yawned. "You'll have to go home and find out for yourself," he replied.

4
00:00:21.258 --> 00:00:24.520
Bobby turned to leave, when Huey said,

5
00:00:24.521 --> 00:00:28.105
"Aren't you forgetting something?"

6
00:00:28.106 --> 00:00:32.015
Bobby scratched his head and looked around.

7
00:00:32.016 --> 00:00:37.501
"Me," Huey said. He pointed to the well.

8
00:00:37.502 --> 00:00:43.458
Bobby put Huey's shell back into the bucket and lowered him down.

9
00:00:43.459 --> 00:00:50.298
Then without a thank you or good-bye, Bobby ran back home as fast as he could.

10
00:00:50.299 --> 00:00:55.693
"Hello? Cy? Panther? Jane?"

11
00:00:55.694 --> 00:01:01.173
Bobby called out the names of his brother and sisters as he ran into the house.

12
00:01:01.174 --> 00:01:04.143
No one answered.

13
00:01:04.144 --> 00:01:08.221
Bobby ran up to the room he shared with Cy.

14
00:01:08.222 --> 00:01:10.907
There was only one bed.

15
00:01:10.908 --> 00:01:13.385
Then he ran to the girls' room.

16
00:01:13.386 --> 00:01:16.485
That room was filled with old boxes and books.

17
00:01:16.486 --> 00:01:21.268
"Yippie!" Bobby shouted gleefully.

18
00:01:21.269 --> 00:01:25.437
He danced around, rejoicing that he was alone.

19
00:01:25.438 --> 00:01:30.811
Bobby had often wondered what it would be like to have no brothers or sisters.

20
00:01:30.812 --> 00:01:34.704
Never having to share, wait, or take turns.

21
00:01:34.705 --> 00:01:39.904
"Now no one can tell me what to do!" he said aloud.

22
00:01:39.905 --> 00:01:42.214
"What do you think you're doing?"

23
00:01:42.215 --> 00:01:45.074
a voice from behind said sharply.

24
00:01:45.075 --> 00:01:48.715
Bobby whirled around to face his aunt.

25
00:01:48.716 --> 00:01:51.959
He ran and gave her a hug.

26
00:01:51.960 --> 00:01:56.666
"Aunt Martha! Am I glad to see you!" he said.

27
00:01:56.667 --> 00:01:58.821
"What's the matter with you?

28
00:01:58.822 --> 00:02:02.540
Are you feeling all right?" asked Aunt Martha.

29
00:02:02.541 --> 00:02:05.677
She put her hand on Bobby's forehead.

30
00:02:05.678 --> 00:02:10.362
"I'm perfectly fine," laughed Bobby.

31
00:02:10.363 --> 00:02:16.823
"Glad to hear it," replied Aunt Martha, "because we've got a lot to do."

32
00:02:16.824 --> 00:02:19.937
She handed Bobby the vacuum cleaner.

33
00:02:19.938 --> 00:02:24.029
"You can start by vacuuming the living room downstairs.

34
00:02:24.030 --> 00:02:26.631
Don't miss any spots!"

35
00:02:26.632 --> 00:02:32.536
"Okay, Aunt Martha," Bobby answered, a little less happy.

36
00:02:32.537 --> 00:02:37.658
As Bobby vacuumed the living room, a memory popped into his head.

37
00:02:37.659 --> 00:02:42.043
He and Cy used to pretend that the vacuum was a monster.

38
00:02:42.044 --> 00:02:44.336
Cy would chase him around shouting,

39
00:02:44.337 --> 00:02:47.392
"He's going to suck you up!"

40
00:02:47.393 --> 00:02:51.181
Bobby had to admit that his brother wasn't always bad.

41
00:02:51.182 --> 00:02:54.382
They did have some fun times together.

42
00:02:54.383 --> 00:02:56.626
Aunt Martha walked in.

43
00:02:56.627 --> 00:02:58.818
"What's taking you so long?"

44
00:02:58.819 --> 00:03:02.579
she said, putting on her coat.

45
00:03:02.580 --> 00:03:07.358
"Well, I, uh . . . ," stuttered Bobby.

46
00:03:07.359 --> 00:03:09.536
Aunt Martha shook her head.

47
00:03:09.537 --> 00:03:12.171
"Never mind," she said.

48
00:03:12.172 --> 00:03:13.587
"Get your jacket.

49
00:03:13.588 --> 00:03:15.756
We're going to Mr. Keefer's."

50
00:03:15.757 --> 00:03:19.958
Mr. Keefer owned the little grocery in town.

51
00:03:19.959 --> 00:03:26.760
Panther and Jane used to love going there because Mr. Keefer always gave them candy.

52
00:03:26.761 --> 00:03:32.329
Whenever the girls got home, Jane would always show off her candy to her brothers.

53
00:03:32.330 --> 00:03:34.969
"Yummy! My favorite!"

54
00:03:34.970 --> 00:03:39.447
she would say, popping a cherry candy into her mouth.

55
00:03:39.448 --> 00:03:42.837
But Panther would hold out the bag to Bobby and say,

56
00:03:42.838 --> 00:03:46.340
"Here, Bobby, take some of mine."

57
00:03:46.342 --> 00:03:53.417
Bobby walked fast to keep up with Aunt Martha as they headed toward the grocery.

58
00:03:53.418 --> 00:03:56.189
"I'm going to get the vegetables,"

59
00:03:56.190 --> 00:03:59.729
Aunt Martha said when they got to Mr. Keefer's.

60
00:03:59.730 --> 00:04:01.506
"Here is the list.

61
00:04:01.507 --> 00:04:06.013
You get the other things and I'll meet you at the cashier."

62
00:04:06.014 --> 00:04:09.106
Bobby looked helplessly at the list.

63
00:04:09.107 --> 00:04:11.810
"But . . . ," he began.

64
00:04:11.811 --> 00:04:15.715
But Aunt Martha had already disappeared down an aisle.

65
00:04:15.716 --> 00:04:20.453
"Unsweetened canned corn," read Bobby.

66
00:04:20.454 --> 00:04:26.280
He searched up and down the aisle but could not figure out where to go.

67
00:04:26.281 --> 00:04:31.433
"If only Panther were here," he said under his breath.

68
00:04:31.434 --> 00:04:36.357
"She would know where everything is."

